
Playwright - webbased functional automation tool
Web based - desktop, mobile - web-view apps [ which works on browser] and doesnt support mobile native apps
Supports - javascript, typescript, java, python, c#/.net
Most popular after 2020 & Very easy installation
Browser supports - Chromium based browser, Webkit - safari.
OS Supports - Windows, Mac, Linux & CLI [ Commad line interpretter]

Feature of Playwright - Open source free automation tool 
                      - Functional, API & Accessibility testing [need 3rd party plugpin]
                      - Supports CI/CD & Docker
                      - Parallel testing is inbuild [no need 3rd party software like testng]
                      - Auto wait mechanism - in built [ no need to add implict/explict waits in code]
                      - Build in Assertions
                      - Supports multi tab & multi Windows
                      - Supports frames and Shadow DOM elements
                      - Supports paramaterization 
                      - Supports mobile emulator
                      - Fast & relaiable 
How to run test case in Playwright
1. npx Playwright test -- headless mode // run all test in all browser with out head
2. npx playwright test --headed //run all test in all browser with head
3. npx playwright show-report
4. To run specific file - npx playwright test example.javascript
5. To run on specific browser-- npx playwright test --project=Chromium
6. To debug and see each steps of execution and codes -- npx playwright test filename --project=Chromium --headed--debug
7. To create test , we need to import packages from playwright.
    import{test,expect} from '@playwright test';
    async: this command will makes JS to wait coz all methods cannot finish their task immediatly.
    await: makes command waits until it recieves the output from previous command.
    

 1. Locators in playwright  page.Locators('property/xpath/CSS')
   Property
   CSS 
   Xpath   
2. page.getByTitle() : to locate an element by totle attribute
3. Two methods to get the text of an element
  a. innerText()
  b. textContent()
4. To records scripts in playwright  
   cmnd// npx playwright codegen = it enables record tool and browser. [ playwright inspector]
   cmnd// npx playwright codegen -o test/mytest.spec.js = automatically reads/records the code and saves it in a file
   cmnd// npx playwright codegen --target java = records the scrpit in tagereted lang [ex: js,java,python]
   cmnd// npx playwright codegen -b webkit | safari | chromium = record in specific targeted browser
   cmnd// npx playwright codegen --device "iphone 13" = record m-web in targeted mobile

5. Assertions 
   --> test assertion is a form of expect function [actual exection is matching with the expected result]
   --> two types of Assertions
      a. Hard - auto - await
      b. Soft - auto - await
      c. JS based assertions - non auto
      d. playwright assertions starts with await which bring auto await to each element across scripts
      e. JS assertions - starts with expect and it doesnot supports auto awaits.
      f. Page based assertions
          (i) toHaveTitle()
          (ii) toHaveURL()
  Hard & Soft Assertions
   Hard - If one line of execution fails it will not continue to next line
   soft - Waits for execution if it fails it skips that and execute all other passed cases
 6. Time outs
    a. defualt timeout 30000ms- 30s it waits for each element  
    b. test.use{timeout:5000} - hard time out for 5 seconds  

 7. Dropdown
     --> In playwright we have diff type to handle Dropdown
         a. label
         b. visible text       
8. Screenshot 
 


9. Reports - list, html, JSON, 3rd party[Allure]

Allure Report - 
a. Install - npm i -D @playwright/test allure-playwright
b. Install comndline- npm install -g allure-commandline --save-dev
c. generate allure report - allure generate allure-results -o allure-report --clean
d. show report - allure open allure-report
e. record screenshot and video for failures , add few config in playwright.config
      - trace: 'on-first-retry',
      - screenshot:"only-on-failure",
      - videos:"on"  

